1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,640
We would do whatever we have to to make students feel safe.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:10,380
In the past week, we've seen thousands of students here at the state capitol asking us to do one thing,

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:13,380
and that is to ban assault weapons.

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:21,280
Nowhere in this bill do I hear the word, or do I see the word, guns, AR-15s, assault weapons,

5
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:26,260
the things that actually are traumatizing and terrorizing these young people.

6
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:33,840
And so my question to the sponsor is that this bill seems to be a Band-Aid.

7
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:39,740
It seems to be a white flag of surrender when what we need to make our young people safe

8
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:46,160
is a deep surgery of our system that places firearms above the lives of our children.

9
00:00:48,430 --> 00:00:52,270
If I may, Mr. Speaker, I want to read from Jeremiah 614 that says,

10
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:54,390
Representative Jones, that's outside the caption.

11
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:56,570
You need to stay on the caption of the bill.

12
00:00:56,570 --> 00:01:02,090
I'm sorry, but you have to stay within the discussion on the bill that is outside.

13
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:05,850
So if you would like to address questions or talk about school safety, that is welcome.

14
00:01:06,290 --> 00:01:06,830
Representative Jones.

15
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:07,790
Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

16
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:12,510
They offer superficial treatments for my people's mortal wound.

17
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:15,010
They give assurances of peace when there is no peace.

18
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:19,430
Representative Jones, once again, that is not on the topic of the bill.

19
00:01:19,610 --> 00:01:21,470
Even your colleagues are nodding yes.

20
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:25,490
I'm asking you again, please stay on the topic of the bill.

21
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:31,930
If you have questions or statements based on that topic of the bill, then please continue.

22
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:34,310
You're recognized, Representative Jones.

23
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:35,290
Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

24
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:38,910
Mr. Speaker, the point I'm trying to make is that this bill is not about school safety.

25
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:40,450
It will not make our students safer.

26
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:43,650
Representative Lambert told the media that we must fortify our schools,

27
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:45,910
even if it means putting tanks outside our schools.

28
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:47,870
That is disturbing.

29
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:51,170
I don't think any of us want to live in a world like that.

30
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:56,830
Well, we make our schools militarized zones simply because we refuse to address the real issue,

31
00:01:57,290 --> 00:02:00,990
which is easy access to military-grade weapons,

32
00:02:01,410 --> 00:02:03,930
which is easy access to weapons of war on our streets.

33
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:10,610
And so, again, I'm deeply troubled that we are making this political statement today

34
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:15,170
by trying to act like we're doing something that is not going to do anything to prevent what occurred.

35
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:17,230
More police officers in schools.

36
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:19,870
Yesterday they passed the bill to armed teachers.

37
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:21,590
This is not going to make our students safe.

38
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:24,230
And I think that we owe it to these young people, the thousands here,

39
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:27,090
who we tried to speak for when we were silenced,

40
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:30,310
the thousands who are gathered outside demanding that we take real action

41
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:34,530
to address the crisis of easy access to military-grade weapons in this state.

42
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:38,130
And so, with that, I must say that I cannot support this bill

43
00:02:38,130 --> 00:02:40,330
because this bill is a Band-Aid.

44
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:41,790
It is a white flag of surrender.

45
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,710
And it is not action that will make our students safe.

46
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:47,090
And no student, I talked to thousands of students,

47
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:49,230
and not one of them said, this is what we want.

48
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:52,070
And I think that we as elected officials have a moral responsibility

49
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:54,710
to listen to these young people who are on the front lines,

50
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:58,010
who are terrified, who are here crying and pleading for their lives.

51
00:02:58,370 --> 00:03:00,550
And so, my question is to the sponsor,

52
00:03:01,370 --> 00:03:04,430
would you be willing to add some provision

53
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:08,490
or to have a conversation about banning assault weapons

54
00:03:08,490 --> 00:03:10,010
to move our state forward?

55
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:11,190
That's what these young people are asking.

56
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:13,010
Would you be willing to do that, Chairman White?

57
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:17,150
Representative Jones, Chairman White.

58
00:03:18,230 --> 00:03:19,550
Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

59
00:03:21,290 --> 00:03:23,170
Representative Jones, look at me.

60
00:03:24,150 --> 00:03:25,650
Look at the other 97.

61
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:30,630
This is exactly what we're trying to do.

62
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:33,910
I have been up here 14 years.

63
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:38,630
You have been in this assembly for two months, three months.

64
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:45,650
We as a legislative body are constantly looking for ideas.

65
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:50,750
But when things break down where we cannot continue

66
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:56,310
to create and discuss ideas, this is where we get to,

67
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:57,830
and this is what has led to this day.

68
00:03:57,830 --> 00:04:00,310
I used to be a school principal.

69
00:04:01,390 --> 00:04:04,470
I would literally step in front of anything

70
00:04:04,470 --> 00:04:07,030
for the protection of those little ones in my school.

71
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:14,170
You assume that because we do not have everything that you may want

72
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,350
or anyone else may want this bill,

73
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:17,990
that this is a bad bill.

74
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:21,890
We are trying to put things together to a starting place.

75
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:24,810
So I answer your question with this.

76
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:29,070
Yes, we've been trying to communicate with you

77
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:32,870
and others on this floor since January.

78
00:04:34,150 --> 00:04:35,410
And here we are today.

79
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:37,170
We have a good bill.

80
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,150
And if you would work with us,

81
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:41,490
we could have even a better bill in the future.

82
00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:43,930
That is my response to you.

83
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,880
Out of order.

84
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:48,780
Out of order.

85
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,320
I got you, Leader Camper.

86
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:50,880
Thank you.

87
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,680
Representative Jones, you're recognized.

88
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,760
Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

89
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,880
To my colleague, Chairman White.

90
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,020
Sorry, the five minutes are up.

91
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,060
Representative Hardaway.

92
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:04,250
Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

93
00:05:04,910 --> 00:05:06,010
Mr. Speaker.

94
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:09,310
Thank you to the gentleman in the well.

95
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:20,300
And thank you for making an attempt at providing a safe environment for our children and our staff

96
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,840
and the visitors to the schools.

97
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:27,520
And I agree that this is only one step.

98
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:34,160
But my concern is it addresses symptoms, that it doesn't address the problems.

99
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:40,400
And as Chairman White said, we've got to do better bills in the future,

100
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:50,000
especially in the case of mental health for our students, for staff, for teachers,

101
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,380
because everything that we're dealing with now has traumatized all of the above.

102
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:59,940
And that's not even mentioning.

103
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:00,280
Thank you.

